# Coding Style

`AGENTS.md` is the source of truth. Follow these on every change.

## Required

* Modular and reusable: small single-purpose units; share via `packages/core`, `packages/shared`, `packages/providers`.
* Simple and straightforward: linear control flow, plain names, fail fast; clarity over cleverness.
* No bloat: no speculative features, unused wrappers, dead code, or “just in case” options.
* No redundancy: extract duplicated logic; never copy tenant/auth/RAG rules across handlers or services.
* Shortest correct readable implementation. Abstract only at real provider/domain boundaries or after a second real use.

## Planning

* Break work into the smallest useful tasks; implement one clear outcome at a time.
* Prefer many small shippable steps over one large change.
* Plan briefly → do the next smallest task → verify → continue.
* Do not mix unrelated refactors into the current task.

## Do not

* Add layers that only forward calls.
* Generalize from a single call site.
* Leave commented-out alternatives or unused dependencies.
* Batch a whole feature vertical when a thinner next step exists.

## Frontend (`apps/web`)

* Keep UI phone- and iPad-friendly on every change (see `frontend-responsive.mdc` / `AGENTS.md`).
